<meta type=book>
<title | A Short Book on Enscribe>
<subtitle | Demonstrating Phase 4 Book Structuring>
<author | The Enscribe Team>
</meta>

<config number-sections />

<preface | About this Book>
This preface introduces the book.<note | A preface footnote.>

<chapter | Introduction>
This is the introduction chapter. It contains some figures, equations,
and footnotes that should collect at the chapter's end.

<fig #fig:intro src=intro.png | An introductory diagram.>

<$$ #eqn:intro | E = mc^2 $$>

A reference to <ref @fig:intro> should resolve to "figure 1.1"
(chapter 1, figure 1).<note | An introduction footnote.>

A second reference to <ref @eqn:intro> should resolve to
"equation 1.1".<note | Another intro footnote.>

<chapter | Methods>
<author | Guest Author>
This chapter has its own author distinct from the book-level author.
The chapter contains its own figure and equation, which should be
numbered starting from 1 in this chapter.

<fig #fig:method src=method.png | The methodology diagram.>

<$$ #eqn:method | F = ma $$>

Cross-reference <ref @fig:method> resolves to "figure 2.1"
(chapter 2, figure 1).<note | A methods footnote.>

A cross-chapter reference: <ref @fig:intro> should still resolve
correctly to "figure 1.1" from this chapter (the prefix path
identifies the target's chapter, not the reference's location).

<appendix | Notation>
This appendix appears in book-back. Its footnotes also collect per-
chapter (per-book-part, more precisely).<note | An appendix footnote.>
